"surface":"அண்ணல்","parts":[{"text":"அண்ணல்","lemma":"அண்ணல்","gloss":"majestic"}],"gloss":"majestic"},{"surface":"யானை","parts":[{"text":"யானை","lemma":"யானை","gloss":"elephant"}],"gloss":"elephant"},{"surface":"அடுகளத்து","parts":[{"text":"அடுகளத்து","lemma":"அடுகளத்து","gloss":"on the battlefield"}],"gloss":"on the battlefield","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"ஒழிய","parts":[{"text":"ஒழி","lemma":"ஒழி","gloss":"stay behind"},{"text":"அ","lemma":"அ","gloss":"infinitive suffix"}],"gloss":"to be left behind"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"அருமை","parts":[{"text":"அருமை","lemma":"அருமை","gloss":"difficulty/preciousness"}],"gloss":"difficult"},{"surface":"சமம்","parts":[{"text":"சமம்","lemma":"சமம்","gloss":"battle"}],"gloss":"battle"},{"surface":"ததைய","parts":[{"text":"ததை","lemma":"ததை","gloss":"shatter"},{"text":"அ","lemma":"அ","gloss":"infinitive suffix"}],"gloss":"to shatter"},{"surface":"நூறி","parts":[{"text":"நூறு","lemma":"நூறு","gloss":"crush"},{"text":"இ","lemma":"இ","gloss":"past participle suffix"}],"gloss":"having crushed"},{"surface":"நீ","parts":[{"text":"நீ","lemma":"நீ","gloss":"you"}],"gloss":"you"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"பெருமை","parts":[{"text":"பெருமை","lemma":"பெருமை","gloss":"greatness"}],"gloss":"great"},{"surface":"தகை","parts":[{"text":"தகை","lemma":"தகை","gloss":"dignity"}],"gloss":"dignity"},{"surface":"விழு","parts":[{"text":"விழு","lemma":"விழு","gloss":"excellent"}],"gloss":"glorious"},{"surface":"புண்","parts":[{"text":"புண்","lemma":"புண்","gloss":"wound"}],"gloss":"wound"},{"surface":"பட்ட","parts":[{"text":"பட்ட","lemma":"பட்ட","gloss":"sustained"}],"gloss":"sustained","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"மாறு","parts":[{"text":"மாறு","lemma":"மாறு","gloss":"manner/because"}],"gloss":"because"},{"surface":"ஏ","parts":[{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"indeed"}]}],"literal":"When the strong-bound drum resounds with an 'iḻum' sound, / going and conquering in battle is what? Those who came / are unable to even withstand your vanguard, and being terrified, / fleeing is practiced by those kings who lack greatness. / Embracing the body of those who died due to disease, / forgetting their love, in order to destroy their sins, / the first of the four Vedas who practice righteousness, / having spread the fresh grass in a proper manner and laid them down, / saying 'may they go to the place where warriors wearing long anklets go, who fell in good battle with valor as their support', / even burying them after splitting them with a sword, they escaped! / While majestic elephants with musth fluid entering their mouths, where striped bees buzz, are left behind on the battlefield, / you crushed the difficult battle so that it shattered, / because you sustained a glorious wound of great dignity!","translation":"When the tightly bound war drums thunder with a deep roar, conquering the battlefield is an easy feat for you. The enemies who march against you cannot even withstand your vanguard; struck with terror, those pride-lacking kings are accustomed only to fleeing. When such ordinary men die of disease, their kin, forgetting their love, lay their bodies on sacred green grass spread by the righteous sages of the four Vedas. To cleanse them of the ignominy of a non-heroic death, they split their bodies with a sword, saying, 'May they reach the high heaven of the brave warriors who fell in glorious battle.' But those kings have escaped that fate! For you, while majestic elephants with streaming musth buzzed by striped bees lay fallen on the battlefield, you crushed the fierce enemy forces and shattered them, receiving a glorious wound of great honor on your chest!","modern":"வலிய கட்டுகளைக் கொண்ட முரசம் 'இழும்' என்று முழங்க, பகைவரைச் சென்று வெல்வது உனக்கு மிக எளிய செயலாகும். உன்னை எதிர்த்து வந்த பகைவர்கள் உன் படைமுன்னணியைத் தாங்க மாட்டாமல், அச்சமுற்று ஓடுவதையே வழக்கமாகக் கொண்ட பெருமையற்ற மன்னர்கள் ஆவர். அவர்கள் போர்க்களத்தில் இறக்காமல் நோயினால் இறக்கும்போது, அவர்களுடைய சுற்றத்தார் அவர்கள் மீதான அன்பை மறந்து, அவர்களின் பாவத்தைப் போக்குவதற்காக, அறநெறி போற்றும் நான்மறை அந்தணர்கள் முறைப்படி பரப்பிய தர்பைப் புல்லின் மேல் அவர்களைக் கிடத்துவர். 'நெடிய வீரக்கழல் அணிந்து, வீரத்தையே பற்றுகோடாகக் கொண்டு போரில் வீழ்ந்த வீரர்கள் செல்லும் துறக்க உலகிற்கு இவர்களும் செல்லட்டும்' என்று கூறி, அவர்களின் உடலை வாளால் பிளந்து அடக்கம் செய்யும் சடங்கிலிருந்து அவர்கள் தப்பினர். வண்டுகள் மொய்க்கும் மதநீர் வழியும் முகத்தையுடைய சிறந்த யானைகள் போர்க்களத்தில் மடியுமாறு, அரிய போரைச் சிதறடித்து வென்ற பெருந்தகையே! நீயோ மார்பில் சிறந்த விழுப்புண்ணைப் பெற்று விளங்குகிறாய்!","explanation":"This poem is set in the Vaakai tinai (victory) and belongs to the Arasa Vaakai turai, celebrating the martial glory of King Atiyaman Netuman Anci, addressed by the famous poet Avvaiyar. The poet contrasts the cowardly enemies who flee the battlefield and die of disease with the heroic Atiyaman who stands tall and receives a glorious wound in battle. In ancient Tamil society, it was considered shameful for a king or warrior to die of disease or old age; hence, the bodies of such kings were symbolically cut with a sword over sacred grass by priests to grant them a warrior's passage to heaven. Avvaiyar notes that Atiyaman's enemies 'escaped' this artificial ritual because they fled, whereas Atiyaman earned his true warrior's passage by sustaining a glorious wound (viluppun) on his chest while crushing the enemy's elephant forces. The imagery of the musth-flowing elephants and the contrast between the ritualistic sword-cut and the actual battlefield wound highlight the supreme valor of the king.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}